Why can't you use gdb? A DJGPP port is available.

>With "-g" do you mean the Makefile options? 

"-g" is a flag to gcc. You have to set it in the Makefile.

>By now I read all the gdb help and info I could get on breakpoints on 
>so on, but I still don't know how to set them, as gdb asks for an 
>address of some kind, but how am I to know where the problem may lie?

Write "help break" at the gdb prompt to get a short help on how to set
breakpoints. For example, if you suspect that the problem might be in
function, say, mkportal() in mkmaze.c, set the breakpoint with "break
mkportal".

You might also want to print debug info during the game with pline() or
write information into a file for later inspection, if you have a better
idea on where the problem might be.

